ber of the <a href="https://docs.microsoft.com/windows/desktop/api/winsock2/ns-winsock2-wsanetworkevents">WSANETWORKEVENTS</a> structure indicates which of the FD_XXX network events have occurred. The <b>iErrorCode</b> array is used to contain any associated error codes with the array index corresponding to the position of event bits in <b>lNetworkEvents</b>. Identifiers such as FD_READ_BIT and FD_WRITE_BIT can be used to index the <b>iErrorCode</b> array. Note that only those elements of the <b>iErrorCode</b> array are set that correspond to the bits set in <i>lNetworkEvents</i> parameter. Other parameters are not modified (this is important for backward compatibility with the applications that are not aware of new FD_ROUTING_INTERFACE_CHANGE and FD_ADDRESS_LIST_CHANGE events). The following error codes can be returned along with the corresponding network event. <b>Event: FD_CONNECT</b></para>
